{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/main/schema/mbmap-2.schema.json",
  "mbmap": 2,
  "vendor": "ComAp",
  "model": "InteliGen4",
  "models": [
    "InteliGen4 200"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "comap-control.com",
  "description": "Gen-set controller: the fixed Modbus registers (clock, command interface for engine start/stop, fault and horn reset and breakers, alarm list, remote control registers). Measured values and setpoints are mapped per configuration.",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "ComAp, InteliGen4 200 Global Guide, SW version 2.2.0, chapter 6 (Modbus)",
  "firmware": "SW version 2.2.0 (the version the guide applies to)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "InteliGen4 200 Global Guide",
      "version": "SW version 2.2.0",
      "url": "https://www.comap-control.com/productfile/4aa6341a-0ba7-4064-8404-3d048728c9bd",
      "note": "chapter 6, Modbus: address space, data types, reserved registers, commands",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "d2302e507333dc98a55909673a96e7ad2c1af8771d331591081daa8463c6ca2e"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU and Modbus/TCP. Addresses are register addresses, from 0 (the guide's 44208 is register 4207).",
    "Binary objects (0-999), values (1000-2999) and setpoints (3000-3999) are mapped by the controller configuration: export the table of Modbus registers from InteliConfig for a given controller. Only the reserved registers, which have the same meaning in every controller, are in this map.",
    "32-bit values are two registers, most significant byte first. Do not use setpoints for regulation; write the remote control registers instead.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's guide; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp+rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
  "registers": [
    {
      "name": "RTC time",
      "group": "Reserved registers",
      "area": "holding",
      "address": 4200,
      "type": "uint32",
      "access": "RW",
      "description": "BCD: high register = hh (high byte) and mm (low byte), low register = ss (high byte), low byte 0."
    },
    {
      "name": "RTC date",
      "group": "Reserved registers",
      "area": "holding",
      "address": 4202,
      "type": "uint32",
      "access": "RW",
      "description": "BCD: high register = dd (high byte) and mm (low byte), low register = yy (high byte), low byte 0."
    },
    {
      "name": "Language index",
      "group": "Reserved registers",
      "area": "holding",
      "address": 4204,
      "type": "uint16",
      "access": "RW",
      "description": "Language of text data given over Modbus (for example alarm list messages)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Last application error",
      "group": "Reserved registers",
      "area": "holding",
      "address": 4205,
      "type": "uint32",
      "access": "R",
      "description": "Read after the device answers with exception code 04; gives the reason."
    },
    {
      "name": "Command argument / return value",
      "group": "Commands",
      "area": "holding",
      "address": 4207,
      "type": "uint32",
      "access": "RW",
      "enum": {
        "0x01FE0000": "Engine start (code 1)",
        "0x02FD0000": "Engine stop (code 1)",
        "0x08F70000": "Fault reset (code 1)",
        "0x04FB0000": "Horn reset (code 1)",
        "0x11EE0000": "GCB toggle (code 2)",
        "0x11EF0000": "GCB on (code 2)",
        "0x11F00000": "GCB off (code 2)",
        "0x12ED0000": "MCB toggle (code 2)",
        "0x12EE0000": "MCB on (code 2)",
        "0x12EF0000": "MCB off (code 2)",
        "0x00000001": "Error: invalid argument",
        "0x00000002": "Error: command refused"
      },
      "description": "Write the argument with function 16, then the command code to 4209 with function 6, then read the return value here. A command that ran returns the value listed in the guide (engine start returns 0x000001FF, GCB on 0x000011F0); 1 and 2 are errors."
    },
    {
      "name": "Command code",
      "group": "Commands",
      "area": "holding",
      "address": 4209,
